# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the Swift evaluation window (tp4/swift; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/swift and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-swift-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint with its own converted-weight directory (never the base's); a job without them is the base,
# byte for byte what production serves.
# SA1 (EXACTNESS of the fast path on Swift's weights, SOFT, the lowest value of the window: cut it first): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-audit, the
# candidate with EVERY audit on (the ship-4 audited attach, its A1), on Swift. The fast path's exactness evidence (the packed-any records, the W2, engine reuse and fusion
# audits) was made on the base's weights; the engine is the same code on tensors of the same shape, so the argument carries over, and this job is the card check of it:
# every audit compares the served composition against the sequential one on device and logs exact=True or a mismatch. warmup, coding, parked_turns, the solo prefill ladder
# and concurrent8_steady. An audited 8x262k profile costs about 8.4 minutes per request. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED. READ as the ship-4 pack's A1
# (references/fusion-jobs/ship4/A1-s4-audited-attach.env): every audit line exact=True, no "audit mismatch", no "fell back", no stall, plus CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow
# passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=...
# weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: created|found" line, and the worker's "[QWEN-C2]
# checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. Duration (estimate): 110 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,parked_turns,prefill_ladder_solo,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
